WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.549 --> 00:00:15.109
Game of Thrones prequel series, House of the
Dragon,

00:00:15.109 --> 00:00:18.470
although based on the George RR Martin's Targaryen
history book Fire &amp; Blood,

00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:22.119
will not feature only Targaryens, but many
other houses

00:00:22.119 --> 00:00:25.890
and many other legendary figures from that
time period as well.

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:30.480
House of the Dragon is a Game of Thrones prequel
show that is confirmed by HBO’s president

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:34.650
to air in 2022.
Miguel Sapochnik and Ryan Condal will serve

00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:39.890
as showrunners and executive producers. George
R. R. Martin will also serve as executive

00:00:39.890 --> 00:00:42.500
producer.
It is based on George RR Martin’s book Fire

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:47.350
And Blood volume 1 and on Martin’s yet unfinished
Fire And Blood volume 2 book.

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:51.800
“Fire &amp; Blood begins their tale with the
legendary Aegon the Conqueror, creator of

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:56.449
the Iron Throne, and goes on to recount the
generations of Targaryens who fought to hold

00:00:56.449 --> 00:01:01.559
that iconic seat, all the way up to the civil
war that nearly tore their dynasty apart.”

00:01:01.559 --> 00:01:05.920
That's Fire And Blood volume 1.
The yet unreleased Fire And Blood volume 2

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:11.840
will continue from where part 1 ended, with
Rhaenyra Targaryen's son Aegon lll's reign

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:17.039
and will cover Blackyre rebellions, war with
Dorne and go all the way to the Mad King and

00:01:17.039 --> 00:01:21.539
Robert's Rebellion that ended Targaryen dynasty.
The key event of the show is also the key

00:01:21.539 --> 00:01:26.040
in the history of House Targaryen, the Dance
of the Dragons - the Targaryen civil war,

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:30.460
which divided the entire kingdom
and launched a huge war that was fought from

00:01:30.460 --> 00:01:35.200
129 AC to 131 AC.
The Dance of the Dragons was the most devastating

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:39.940
war in the history of the Seven Kingdoms.
A war of succession between Aegon II and his

00:01:39.940 --> 00:01:44.099
half-sister Rhaenyra over their father Viserys
I's throne.

00:01:44.099 --> 00:01:48.020
Both of them thought they belonged on the
Iron Throne. When people started declaring

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:52.039
for one of them or the other, their fight
divided the kingdoms in two.

00:01:52.039 --> 00:01:57.489
Targaryens fought Targaryens, bothers fought
brothers, dragons fought dragons. By the time

00:01:57.489 --> 00:02:01.840
it was over, thousands were dead.
Cregan Stark, known as the Old Man of the

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:05.599
North, The Wolf of the North and The Wolf
of Winterfell, was the Lord of Winterfell

00:02:05.599 --> 00:02:09.009
and the head of House Stark during the Targaryn
civil war.

00:02:09.009 --> 00:02:13.110
A huge Northman with a hard face, dressed
in fur and iron,

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:17.320
Lord Cregan was a pillar of strength and his
presence by itself would command fear and

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:20.340
respect.
He briefly ruled Kings Landing in the Hour

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:24.050
of the Wolf
when he brought order and justice to the capital

00:02:24.050 --> 00:02:29.000
and served as Hand of the King for Aegon III
after the Dance of the Dragons.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:34.250
Cregan Stark was born in 108 AC, the eldest
son of Lord Rickon Stark and Lady Gilliane

00:02:34.250 --> 00:02:36.870
Glover.
Cregan became the Lord of Winterfell and the

00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:43.810
Warden of the North in 121 AC at the age of
thirteen, when his lord father passed away.

00:02:43.810 --> 00:02:48.640
During his minority, his uncle Bennard ruled
the north as a regent. When Cregan turned

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:55.250
sixteen and came of age in 124 AC, Bennard
was slow to surrender his power. Relations

00:02:55.250 --> 00:02:59.680
between Cregan and Bennard grew strained
as the young Lord of Winterfell chafed under

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:04.330
the limits imposed on him by his uncle.
Before fighting someone else's war, Cregan

00:03:04.330 --> 00:03:07.569
had to fight his own war to get what was rightfully
his,

00:03:07.569 --> 00:03:10.690
to take the rule of the North from his uncle
upon himself.

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:16.740
3 years before the Dance of the Dragons started,
in 126 AC, Cregan finally rose up against

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:20.360
his uncle,
and imprisoned Bennard and his three sons,

00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:23.200
taking the rule of the North into his own
hands.

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:28.209
Upon the death of King Viserys I Targaryen,
Rhaenyra's son Prince Jacaerys Velaryon flew

00:03:28.209 --> 00:03:31.790
to Winterfell on his dragon Vermax to gain
the support of the Starks

00:03:31.790 --> 00:03:35.470
and the north for his mother Rhaenyra Targaryen's
claim to the Iron Throne.

00:03:35.470 --> 00:03:40.410
The alliance, known as the Pact of Ice and
Fire, stated that a Targaryen princess,

00:03:40.410 --> 00:03:44.550
the future firstborn daughter of Jacaerys,
would marry his son Rickon.

00:03:44.550 --> 00:03:49.100
Cregan pledged his support to the blacks during
the Dance of the Dragons.

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:54.060
Cregan had a bastard half-sister, and Mushroom's
ribald account of the war claims that Jacaerys

00:03:54.060 --> 00:03:58.540
fell in love with and secretly married the
girl at Winterfell's Godswood.

00:03:58.540 --> 00:04:03.220
After Prince Jacaerys Velaryon secured the
allegiance of the North for his mother Rhaenyra

00:04:03.220 --> 00:04:08.080
Targaryen, Lord Cregan Stark sent two thousand
soldiers known as the Winter Wolves south

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:12.660
commanded by his bannerman Lord Roderick Dustin
known as Roddy the Ruin to support the Queen's

00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:16.150
claim while he remained in the North to gather
his own banners

00:04:16.150 --> 00:04:20.180
(due to the vastness of the North this would
take long).

00:04:20.180 --> 00:04:24.680
The Winter Wolves were grizzled soldiers who
rode shaggy northern horses,

00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:31.580
wore old mail and ragged skins, wielded axes,
mauls, spiked maces and ancient iron swords.

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:35.610
It was long the custom in the north for older
men to leave their homes in winter

00:04:35.610 --> 00:04:38.849
and thereby preserve supplies for their younger
kin,

00:04:38.849 --> 00:04:43.360
so the Winter Wolves expected they would die
while marching for glory, adventure, and plunder.

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:48.759
''We have come to die for the dragon queen.''
said Lord Roderick while leading 2000

00:04:48.759 --> 00:04:52.919
Winter Wolfs into battle. There is probably
nothing scarier than fighting men who have

00:04:52.919 --> 00:04:56.099
come to die.
During the Battle by the Lakeshore, the Winter

00:04:56.099 --> 00:04:59.800
Wolves led the attack
and charged the Lannister spear men five times,

00:04:59.800 --> 00:05:04.940
with two thirds of the Northmen killed or
wounded in their decisive victory for the

00:05:04.940 --> 00:05:08.229
blacks.
During the Butcher's Ball, Lord Roderick sounded

00:05:08.229 --> 00:05:12.039
the charge of the Winter Wolves
and their river knight allies against Ser

00:05:12.039 --> 00:05:15.169
Criston Cole’s army in the ensuing Butcher's
Ball,

00:05:15.169 --> 00:05:19.389
a slaughter of the greens.
During the First Battle of Tumbleton, the

00:05:19.389 --> 00:05:22.569
surviving Winter Wolves screamed northern
war cries

00:05:22.569 --> 00:05:27.930
and rode from a Postern gate. Despite being
outnumbered by ten to one,

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:32.180
Lord Roderick led the Northmen in a charge
against Lord Ormund Hightower.

00:05:32.180 --> 00:05:36.710
As the singers tell it, Lord Roderick was
blood from head to heel as he came on,

00:05:36.710 --> 00:05:41.020
yet so drunk with a battle that he did not
even seem to feel his wounds.

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:45.750
Lord Ormund's nephew, Ser Bryndon, was able
to cut off Roderick's shield arm with a longaxe,

00:05:45.750 --> 00:05:50.930
but the Northern lord was able to kill both
Hightowers before succumbing to his wounds.

00:05:50.930 --> 00:05:54.210
Rhaenyra fled King's Landing after the Storming
of the Dragonpit.

00:05:54.210 --> 00:05:57.999
While she was staying at Duskendale, Lord
Stark wrote that he would gather for her a

00:05:57.999 --> 00:06:02.930
host of ten thousand Northmen younger and
fiercer than the fallen Winter Wolves.

00:06:02.930 --> 00:06:06.849
Rhaenyra was killed at Dragonstone by King
Aegon II Targaryen, however,

00:06:06.849 --> 00:06:11.279
but Cregan with his army still marched south
nontheless in support of her son,

00:06:11.279 --> 00:06:15.069
Prince Aegon the Younger.
The war continued between the supporters of

00:06:15.069 --> 00:06:20.589
the dead queen and the King's remaining loyalists.
Riverlands, the North and the Vale still supported

00:06:20.589 --> 00:06:25.509
the claim of Rhaenyra's son, Aegon III,
while Aegon II only had the Stormlands army

00:06:25.509 --> 00:06:29.089
able to defend him.
While Lord Stark moved south with his army

00:06:29.089 --> 00:06:34.189
to overthrow Aegon II and place Rhaenyra's
son on the Iron Throne, Lord Borros Baratheon

00:06:34.189 --> 00:06:38.809
was marching north with his own banners,
but he was defeated on the Kingsroad by the

00:06:38.809 --> 00:06:43.069
Riverlords known as the Lads before Lord Stark
arrived.

00:06:43.069 --> 00:06:47.159
Having failed to get the battle he wanted,
Stark nevertheless wanted to punish those

00:06:47.159 --> 00:06:52.229
who had supported Aegon II. He moved his forces
to claim King's Landing where he found that

00:06:52.229 --> 00:06:56.910
Aegon II had been poisoned and Aegon III was
now a king.

00:06:56.910 --> 00:07:02.159
Since he was aged eleven, a regency needed
to be established and several lords were vying

00:07:02.159 --> 00:07:05.199
for power.
With his formidable presence and character

00:07:05.199 --> 00:07:08.889
as well as with his army,
Lord Stark was the most powerful man in King's

00:07:08.889 --> 00:07:11.879
Landing.
With his newfound power, Lord Stark wanted

00:07:11.879 --> 00:07:16.669
to punish those who had supported Aegon II
such as the Baratheons, the Lannisters and

00:07:16.669 --> 00:07:20.029
the Hightowers.
However, Lord Corlys Velaryon had already

00:07:20.029 --> 00:07:23.590
sent envoys to Oldtown, Storm's End and Casterly
Rock

00:07:23.590 --> 00:07:27.550
to make peace. While the word of the envoys
was being waited upon,

00:07:27.550 --> 00:07:33.119
there was another matter that Lord Stark wanted
to deal with: the assassination of Aegon II.

00:07:33.119 --> 00:07:37.610
While he had believed that he had been a usurper
and had been riding south to oust him from

00:07:37.610 --> 00:07:42.770
power, Lord Stark did not believe in killing
him, but rather in defeating him on the field

00:07:42.770 --> 00:07:46.360
of battle.
He declared that all those who had partaken

00:07:46.360 --> 00:07:50.689
in the killing needed to be punished.
His troops arrested several people in the

00:07:50.689 --> 00:07:54.339
capital, including Lord Velaryon, Lord Larys
Strong,

00:07:54.339 --> 00:07:58.349
the Master of Whisperers, and several members
of the Kingsguard.

00:07:58.349 --> 00:08:02.240
After these arrests were made, Lord Stark
was appointed Hand of the King by King Aegon

00:08:02.240 --> 00:08:05.919
III.
During the day that followed his appointment,

00:08:05.919 --> 00:08:10.749
Lord Stark led the trials and execution of
the traitors, sending most to the Wall and

00:08:10.749 --> 00:08:15.960
executing a member of the Kingsguard
and Lord Strong who refused to take the black.

00:08:15.960 --> 00:08:20.839
Following the traditions of House Stark, Lord
Cregan beheaded them both himself with Ice,

00:08:20.839 --> 00:08:25.389
the Valyrian steel greatsword of the Starks.
This event came to be known as the 'Hour of

00:08:25.389 --> 00:08:30.509
the Wolf' or the 'Judgment of the Wolf'.
Lord Velaryon escaped execution or sentence

00:08:30.509 --> 00:08:34.409
when the King issued an edict
that he was to be spared and returned to his

00:08:34.409 --> 00:08:39.580
former dignity as Lord of the Tides.
Cregan married Alysanne Blackwood in exchange

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:45.560
for honoring Aegon III's pardon of Lord Corlys.
Lord Stark resigned as the Hand the following

00:08:45.560 --> 00:08:50.430
day and left King's Landing for Winterfell.
''The snows are falling in the North and my

00:08:50.430 --> 00:08:53.810
place is at Winterfell.''
said Cregan explaining why he cannot stay

00:08:53.810 --> 00:08:57.170
at King's Landing.
It was during Cregan's long reign as Lord

00:08:57.170 --> 00:09:01.480
of Winterfell that House Stark's loyalty to
the Iron Throne (doubtful at best prior to

00:09:01.480 --> 00:09:05.810
this) became a certainty.
King Aegon III Targaryen granted many rewards

00:09:05.810 --> 00:09:08.970
to Cregan,
although a Targaryen princess never married

00:09:08.970 --> 00:09:12.870
into House Stark.
Sometime after the war, Cregan fought with

00:09:12.870 --> 00:09:17.100
Aemon Targaryen the Dragonknight,
The Prince of House Targaryen, member of the

00:09:17.100 --> 00:09:22.220
Kingsguard and one of the greatest swordsmen
of his age and ever in the history of Westeros

00:09:22.220 --> 00:09:26.850
and was only barely defeated.
Aemon claimed he never faced a finer swordsman

00:09:26.850 --> 00:09:30.279
than Lord Cregan.
His name is mentioned within the entry of

00:09:30.279 --> 00:09:35.089
Aemon Targaryen in The Book of Brothers.
Cregan went on to have a long life which earned

00:09:35.089 --> 00:09:40.480
him the nickname of ''the Old Man of the North''.
Cregan was entombed in the crypts of Winterfell.

00:09:40.480 --> 00:09:44.550
Cregan Stark will definitely be one of my
favorite characters in the House of the Dragon.

00:09:44.550 --> 00:09:47.810
An honorable man who upholds his oath to Queen
Rhaenyra

00:09:47.810 --> 00:09:50.910
and whose men, the Winter Wolves fought during
most of the war

00:09:50.910 --> 00:09:55.029
and earned the Blacks quite a few important
victories in the Riverlands.

00:09:55.029 --> 00:09:59.550
Legendary characters such as Cregan Stark,
legendary battles such as the Winter Wolfs'

00:09:59.550 --> 00:10:03.089
charge into the Greens army despite being
outnumbered by ten to one

00:10:03.089 --> 00:10:05.910
and managing to reach the commander of the
greens,

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:08.329
and seeing a Stark rule the capital Kings
Landing,

00:10:08.329 --> 00:10:13.620
of that and more this Game of Thrones prequel
show, House of the Dragon, brings in 2022.

00:10:13.620 --> 00:10:16.630
Let me know your thoughts about all of this
in the comment section down below.

00:10:16.630 --> 00:10:19.000
Thank you so much for watching and hope to
see you in the next one. Peace!

